  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxzbegeels2t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The paper on how a team of Gemini 4 agents beat Minecraft is worth a look.\n\nIt is accessible example (partially because it is AI written & on a popular game) of spontaneous coordination among agents to accomplish a complicated goal & how their approach differs from humans/ arxiv.org/pdf/2610.22319",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mxzbegeels2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-16T19:04:18.196Z",
      "likes": 98,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 11,
      "score": 6.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 21.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxxj65qhac2t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "This paper shows why I am skeptical of the idea that frontier models can be easily replaced by cheaper ones (and why you should use the best models as orchestrators): Small improvements in accuracy & judgement compound over long-horizon tasks, creating huge gains in outcomes and reduction in errors.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mxxj65qhac2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-16T02:18:38.285Z",
      "likes": 132,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 14,
      "score": 6.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 38.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3my3f4q2xic2r",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Anthropic floats a sample bill. It would allow the gov’t to block a model that has a “foreseeable, imminent risk of more than $1 billion in damages, or of killing or seriously injuring more than 50 people”\nwww.politico.com/news/2026/10...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3my3f4q2xic2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-17T15:16:54.381Z",
      "likes": 21,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 6.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.6,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxwf7wo7rs2x",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The sudden collapse of the value of Chain-of-Thought (even summarized CoT) in the agentic era changes working with AI.\n\nEffectively steering AIs and getting any sort of observability now requires you to ask for interim outputs & tests, and to use AI help to troubleshoot problems you find.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mxwf7wo7rs2x",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:35:23.276Z",
      "likes": 60,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 48.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3my3f4qky6k2r",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Snark alert: let me just note that some employees of OpenAI and Anthropic already “foresee” a 10% chance of 8 billion people.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3my3f4qky6k2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-17T15:16:54.382Z",
      "likes": 16,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 5.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxzryjiyik2e",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "It's what happens when the last academic paper one read on neural nets was in 2014 and no one has updated their priors since. It would be hilarious if the rationalist doomerism was predicated on the belief that mechanistic interpretability was a hard thing to do.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mxzryjiyik2e",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-17T00:01:52.451Z",
      "likes": 13,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 5.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 16.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxwdd7562c2w",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "Next week I'm speaking on a panel for open access week about AI and scholarly communication, and I'm going to talk about the ACM digital library. Does anyone have examples of e.g. mistakes in AI summaries, particularly ridiculous \"podcast\" things, etc.?",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mxwdd7562c2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:01:25.334Z",
      "likes": 4,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 4.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 49.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxwf4huoqs2n",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "This is a panel for open access week about scholarly communication. \n\nI have no idea what models ACM is using - if they're not using the \"newest\" and \"best\" that probably just makes it worse.",
